8 #edb/ref 17592186411834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411862 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98330" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411862 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411862 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following curves is simple, closed, and positively oriented?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411862 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "71602977-82c1-5c53-87d8-1a470298d861" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411862 #edb/ref 1074 "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented. \n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise. \n\nAmong the given options, the only positively oriented simple closed curve is the following:\n\n![](images/47/47497b397779489e0685a201a792a36ea2e2755c299063c61403087679442971.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
